{"title":"Clair de Lune","slug":"Clair_de_Lune","hero":null,"pageid":909,"revid":22030,"timestamp":"2026-07-02T09:36:50Z","lastEditor":"Ludicolocynth","categories":["Vinyls"],"infobox":{"type":"Objects","fields":[{"label":"Island","value":"Finlay Island"},{"label":"Shop","value":"The Oak Depot"},{"label":"Price","value":"$600"},{"label":"Function","value":"Plays Music"},{"label":"Version Added","value":"v1.16.0"},{"label":"Date Added","value":"07/03/2023"},{"label":"Status","value":"Obtainable"}]},"sections":[{"id":"description","text":"Description"},{"id":"song","text":"Song"},{"id":"trivia","text":"Trivia"}],"body":"<h2 id=\"description\">Description</h2>\n\n<p><br>\n<b>Clair de Lune</b> is a Vinyl that can be purchased for <span>$600</span> at <a href=\"__BASE__/wiki/The_Oak_Depot/\">The Oak Depot</a>. The Vinyl itself is the real classical piano piece <i><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suite_bergamasque#3._Clair_de_lune\">Clair de lune</a></i> by French composer <a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claude_Debussy\">Claude Debussy</a>.\n</p><p>Some players suggest to make the <i><a target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suite_bergamasque#3._Clair_de_lune\">Clair de lune</a></i> vinyl to be louder since it was too quiet or a little quite.\n</p>\n<h2 id=\"song\">Song</h2>\n<p><span typeof=\"mw:File\"><span role=\"img\" aria-label=\"Media not yet archived: media file\">media file</span></span>\n</p>\n<h2 id=\"trivia\">Trivia</h2>\n<ul><li>Clair de Lune is the baseplate for all other Vinyls as proven in Hoofer's profile.</li></ul>"}
